 - **Game Speed Chart**: similarly a new category to see all game speed XML values in a **sortable chart**, notably **by icons (first column)**, which allows to **group them by theme**. In particular, they allow to see the full **Calendar/Timeline** information in lines such as `"+2*10k=30k"` or `"+40*m2=2076m9"` for each month increment and each game speed; and the **Culture Level Infos** at each game speed. For convenience, additional fields are added (e.g. or `Total Turns*` 165 at game speed Turbo) and marked with `*` to distinguish them from regular XML info fields. Also added **analysis rows** (e.g., `Summary 08 (40%)` with `T200=+1400 (120)`; `Increments Years 02` with `750, 500, 250`; `Increments Months 02` with `9000, 6000, 3000`). See [Sevopedia reworks (Game Speed Chart)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-06-game-speed-chart-category).
 - **World Sizes Chart**: similarly a new category to see all World Size XML values in a **sortable chart**. See [Sevopedia reworks (World Sizes Chart)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-07-world-sizes-chart-category). Similarly, for convenience, additional fields are added (e.g. or `Ratio to Standard*` 3.640 at World Size SAS24), `Ratio to Largest*` (e.g. "0.502" for SAS24 World Size), `Tiles Per Default Player*` (e.g. 145 for World Size Huge), or `Recommended DLL*` (e.g."48 Civs" at World Size SAS24) and marked with `*` to help identify them.
 - Similarly, added a new Eras Chart category with sortable entries including the list of techs for all eras, and notably **optional era buttons**. See [Sevopedia reworks (Eras Chart)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-08-eras-chart-category).
-- New **Media Player** (**shared** between Sevopedia Movies and Music): supports **Replay**, **Eject (Exit)**, **Previous Track** and **Next track**, **Toggle Movies/Music**, **Fast Up** and **Fast Down** (change grouping), **Timer**, and a **Playlist** and a **TV panel** on the right side for **non-bik** files (e.g., for **nif**, **dds**), or **a more compact** queue form **for bik files**. This allows to view without having to exit the screen. Click on **Eject button** or **Right-click** to **stop the media playing**; press Escape or Enter key for main menu. See [Sevopedia reworks (Media Player)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-090-media-player). See also [KI#141](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#141---fixed-sevopedia-media-player-3d-audio-previews-became-very-quiet-after-entering-a-game). Note: Civ selection/action sounds can include several variants. Replay to hear different samples. Note 2: some Improvement 3D sounds as of now can play no or the wrong sound. Try to click Play several times to hear the correct sound. Note 3: Ambience 3D can start late; e.g;, dog begins around 6-9 seconds, and horn beings at around 8-13 seconds (They seem not to start right away, e.g., after entering city screen).
+- New **Media Player** (**shared** between Sevopedia Movies and Music): supports **Replay**, **Eject (Exit)**, **Previous Track** and **Next track**, **Toggle Movies/Music**, **Fast Up** and **Fast Down** (change grouping), **Timer**, and a **Playlist** and a **TV panel** on the right side for **non-bik** files (e.g., for **nif**, **dds**), or **a more compact** queue form **for bik files**. This allows to view without having to exit the screen. Click on **Eject button** or **Right-click** to **stop the media playing**; press Escape or Enter key for main menu. See [Sevopedia reworks (Media Player)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-090-media-player). See also [KI#141](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#141---fixed-sevopedia-media-player-3d-audio-previews-became-very-quiet-after-entering-a-game). Note: Civ selection/action sounds can include several variants. Replay to hear different samples. Note 2: some Improvement 3D sounds as of now can play no or the wrong sound. Try to click Play several times to hear the correct sound. Note 3: Ambience 3D can start late; e.g;, dog begins around 5-20 seconds, and horn beings at around 8-20 seconds (They seem not to start right away, e.g., after entering city screen).
 - New **Movies category** (bik, nif, dds) for **Victories**, **Wonders**, **Projects**, **Religions**, **Corporations** (if any; as of now in base AdvCiv there are none), and **Eras**, additional **audio support for non-bik** files (e.g. Religions have a nif + separate audio asset). **Play button** added in related Sevopedia categories to redirect to their entry in Sevopedia Movies. See [Sevopedia reworks (Movies (with audio support))](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-091-movies-category-with-audio-support).
 - New **Music category**: allows to play **~1750 audio scripts** (i.e. files) in Sevopedia, notably for **Techs**, **Leaders**, **Eras**, **Civilizations**, and many other. **Play button** added in related Sevopedia categories to redirect to Sevopedia Music. Approach broadly similar to that of Sevopedia Movies. **Search bar support** and **widening** allows to find desired tracks. Note: there are **multiple sounds in an item** for each civilization sound item, so **replay many times the same item to hear all civilization sounds**. See [Sevopedia reworks (Music)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-092-music-category-1750-audio-scripts-playable-in-sevopedia).
 - New **Expanded Text Panels** so History/Background **text** (e.g. of the Viking unit that is long and requires scrolling to be seen or of the Great General Unit (that includes uniquenames that require scrolling to be scanned quickly)) easier to read, with **EXPAND** and **CLOSE** buttons. It occupies the whole item's page but **preserves the rest of the sevopedia page display** (footer, header, item bar and category bar) for easy browsing. This allows to **browse other category items** (e.g., other leaders from sevopedia leader's item bar) **without having to close and reopen expanded view** everytime item is changed (e.g. when clicking on another leader). Added as an optional helper shared across all eligible categories (main code in [_sevopedia_helpers.py](/Assets/Python/Contrib/Sevopedia/_sevopedia_helpers.py)). Added optional **Playground** to experiment with **text color**, **background**, and **panel styles**, with `+` and `-` button to swap them and descriptions like `TEXT: PLAYER_LIGHT_BLUE_TEXT (147,188,252,255) (57/129)`,  `BG: MAINMENU_SLIDESHOW_LOAD (2/8)`, and `STYLE: PANEL_STYLE_MAIN_TAN (36/50)`: helps choosing or testing optimal art style without having to tediously manually testing them one by one. See [Sevopedia reworks (Expanded text panel)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-093-expanded-text-panel-with-expand-and-close-buttons).

